From: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: use route device for neighbour xmit

The transmit-path consolidation backported to 6.18.45 uses the discovered
output interface for FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH. Path discovery can select a
bridge port even when the flow retains neighbour-based transmission, whose
neighbour lookup and cached route still refer to the bridge itself.

On the GL-BE9300 with PPPoE WAN and bridged LAN, the reply route uses
br-lan but the stored output index points to lan1. Software-offloaded
HTTPS stalls with this combination. Selecting the cached route device
restores traffic without reverting the common transmit helper or
disabling software offload.

Use the route device for IPv4 and IPv6 neighbour transmission, matching
the device used by the neighbour lookup and the pre-consolidation path.
Leave direct transmission unchanged.

Validated with an ARM64 module build, controlled live IPv4 HTTPS
comparisons, 10 MiB downloads with software offload enabled, and a
user-run speed test. IPv6 runtime validation remains pending; the router
has no IPv6 default route.

Fixes: b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable: consolidate xmit path")
Signed-off-by: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c
@@ -463,7 +463,7 @@ nf_flow_offload_ip_hook(void *priv, stru
 	switch (tuplehash->tuple.xmit_type) {
 	case FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH:
 		rt = dst_rtable(tuplehash->tuple.dst_cache);
-		xmit.outdev = dev_get_by_index_rcu(state->net, tuplehash->tuple.ifidx);
+		xmit.outdev = rt->dst.dev;
 		if (!xmit.outdev) {
 			flow_offload_teardown(flow);
 			return NF_DROP;
@@ -768,7 +768,7 @@ nf_flow_offload_ipv6_hook(void *priv, st
 	switch (tuplehash->tuple.xmit_type) {
 	case FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH:
 		rt = dst_rt6_info(tuplehash->tuple.dst_cache);
-		xmit.outdev = dev_get_by_index_rcu(state->net, tuplehash->tuple.ifidx);
+		xmit.outdev = rt->dst.dev;
 		if (!xmit.outdev) {
 			flow_offload_teardown(flow);
 			return NF_DROP;
